LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
SUMMARY:Writing in the Galleries
DESCRIPTION:Spark your creative writing through close looking and convers
 ation.&#160\;Whether you're a writer or simply curious to try something n
 ew\, you'll find inspiration here and a welcoming community to share the 
 journey.  For this instance\, we'll spark our creativity with a look at t
 he featured exhibition in the Prints\, Drawings\, and Photographs Gallery
 . &#160\;Read about the exhibition. (https://artmuseum.indiana.edu/exhibi
 tions/2027-03-23-chitra-ganesh.html)&#160\;  &#160\;  What to Bringyour f
 avorite pencil (no pens).  a notebook or paper. Clipboards are available 
 to borrow.  a phone or camera to take a picture of the art for later refe
 rence.  Know Before You GoArrive early\, check in\, and get ready for an 
 on-time start.Readwhere to find us\, where to park\, accessibility\, and 
 museum guidelines.About Your Facilitator  Dedaimia Whitney earned an MFA 
 in fiction from Indiana University under the direction of Scott Russell S
 anders. She taught creative writing at Franklin College for many years. S
 he has served the museum as a docent since 2019. Her favorite works of ar
 t are those that are both visually stimulating and thought-provoking.
