LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
SUMMARY:Guided Tour: New on View
DESCRIPTION:Whether it's your first visit or your hundredth\, you'll be i
 nvited to look closely\, share ideas\, and enjoy conversation with fellow
  guests. Each tour is a little different\, featuring a unique selection o
 f artworks and perspectives.  For this instance\, we'll include a look at
  the featured exhibitions: David Smith\, The Forgings: Sculptures\, Drawi
 ngs\, Photographs (https://artmuseum.indiana.edu/exhibitions/2027-02-13-d
 avid-smith-forgings.html) as well as Chitra Ganesh: Impressions of Mythic
  Futures (https://artmuseum.indiana.edu/exhibitions/2027-03-23-chitra-gan
 esh.html)  Tours begin at the Welcome Desk on the first floor and last ap
 proximately 60 minutes. Please arrive on time\, as tours start promptly. 
  This small-group experience is led by Community Guides who are passionat
 e about sharing their love of art and helping guests make meaningful conn
 ections with the museum's collections.  Interested in a private guided ex
 perience for an adult group or a school or youth group? Check out our men
 u of guided experiences. (https://artmuseum.indiana.edu/visit/museum-tour
 s/index.html)  &#160\;  Know Before You GoSpace is available for the firs
 t 12 people to check in with Guest Services on the day. Drop by the infor
 mation desk on the first floor of the museum when you arrive.A small hand
 bag may be carried at your side. Backpacks and large bags will need to be
  stored before touring. Learn more aboutmuseum guidelines.If you park in 
 the IMU parking lot\, Guest Services can validate your parking voucher fo
 r a discount.Read aboutwhere to find us and where to park\,
