LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
SUMMARY:Guided Tour
DESCRIPTION:Whether it's your first visit or your hundredth\, you'll be i
 nvited to look closely\, share ideas\, and enjoy conversation with fellow
  guests. Each tour is a little different\, featuring a unique selection o
 f artworks and perspectives. The topic for this instance is Visual Persua
 sion.&#160\;  Tours begin at the Welcome Desk on the first floor and last
  approximately 60 minutes. Please arrive on time\, as tours start promptl
 y.  This small-group experience is led by Community Guides who are passio
 nate about sharing their love of art and helping guests make meaningful c
 onnections with the museum's collections.  Interested in a private guided
  experience for an adult group or a school or youth group? Check out our 
 menu of guided experiences. (https://artmuseum.indiana.edu/visit/museum-t
 ours/index.html)  &#160\;  About Your Guide:  Helena Walsh has been volun
 teering as a docent and guide at the Eskenazi Museum of Art for more than
  25 years. She enjoys learning about art history and enjoys introducing p
 eople to the art museum and sharing knowledge.  Know Before You GoSpace i
 s available for the first 12 people to check in with Guest Services on th
 e day. Drop by the information desk on the first floor of the museum when
  you arrive.A small handbag may be carried at your side. Backpacks and la
 rge bags will need to be stored before touring. Learn more aboutmuseum gu
 idelines.If you park in the IMU parking lot\, Guest Services can validate
  your parking voucher for a discount.Read aboutwhere to find us and where
  to park\,
